WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.272
mod_wsgi's creator

00:00:02.083 --> 00:00:03.015
is building its

00:00:02.826 --> 00:00:03.970
Rust successor

00:00:04.494 --> 00:00:06.062
Graham Dumpleton started

00:00:05.874 --> 00:00:07.772
mod_wsgi twenty years

00:00:07.584 --> 00:00:08.126
ago

00:00:08.265 --> 00:00:09.455
His new project

00:00:09.303 --> 00:00:09.915
Muru

00:00:09.986 --> 00:00:11.189
is an AI-assisted

00:00:11.001 --> 00:00:11.932
Rust server for

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:13.771
WSGI and ASGI

00:00:13.583 --> 00:00:14.679
Python apps

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:16.239
He has published

00:00:16.051 --> 00:00:16.982
almost a post

00:00:16.794 --> 00:00:17.430
a day for

00:00:17.242 --> 00:00:18.610
three weeks covering

00:00:18.422 --> 00:00:19.070
workers

00:00:19.235 --> 00:00:20.933
HTTPS in development

00:00:20.992 --> 00:00:21.829
Kubernetes

00:00:22.006 --> 00:00:23.303
scaling to zero

00:00:23.115 --> 00:00:24.647
and in-page tracing

00:00:25.166 --> 00:00:25.991
His take

00:00:26.121 --> 00:00:27.076
the AI does

00:00:26.888 --> 00:00:27.524
much of the

00:00:27.336 --> 00:00:28.255
surface work

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:29.316
but deciding what

00:00:29.152 --> 00:00:29.941
isn't good enough

00:00:29.753 --> 00:00:30.531
yet is still

00:00:30.343 --> 00:00:31.109
his job

00:00:31.638 --> 00:00:32.652
Full story on

00:00:32.463 --> 00:00:33.359
the dashboard
